---
title: "Chicken Shawarma Salad"
summary: "One of my absolute favorite salads for the summer"
publishedDate: 2025-08-13
heroImage: /images/recipes/chicken-shawarma-salad.webp
pillar: blood-sugar
cta: book-consult
prepMinutes: 20
cookMinutes: 20
servings: "4"
ingredients:
  - "1 small-medium head iceberg lettuce (thinly sliced)"
  - "1 each medium cucumber (diced)"
  - "1 cup cherry tomatoes (halved)"
  - "1 1/2 Tbsp shallot (minced)"
  - "2 lbs boneless chicken thighs"
  - "1 tsp paprika"
  - "1/2 tsp chili powder"
  - "1 tsp cumin powder"
  - "1 pinch cinnamon"
  - "1 tsp dry thyme"
  - "1 tsp salt"
  - "1/2 tsp black pepper"
  - "2 cloves garlic (minced)"
  - "1 each lemon (juiced)"
  - "1 Tbsp avocado oil"
  - "1/3 cup tahini"
  - "1 each lemon (juiced)"
  - "1 tsp apple cider vinegar"
  - "1 Tbsp extra virgin olive oil"
  - "1/2 tsp garlic granules"
  - "1 pinch salt"
  - "1-3 Tbsp water"
steps:
  - "Trim fat from chicken thighs"
  - "In a large bowl, add chicken and all seasoning, along with lemon juice, garlic and oil."
  - "Marinate for at least 30 minutes or up to overnight."
  - "Heat grill until hot, sear chicken on both sides until browned with grill marks - if grilling, each side should cook about 5-7 minutes, or until internal temperature reaches 165."
  - "Alternatively, use a grill pan on the stovetop. Preheat oven to 350. Heat grill pan and sear chicken until browned on each side, about 5 minutes per side. Transfer to oven for about 5-10 minutes or until internal temperature reaches 165."
  - "Allow to rest for 10 minutes before slicing"
  - "Combine salad vegetables in a large bowl."
  - "In a small mixing bowl combine all dressing ingredients except water. Tahini will thicken as you add the liquids."
  - "Then add water 1 Tbsp at a time and whisk to thin out the dressing to desired thickness - may take more water, just add slowly and whisk until dressing is runny but not too thin."
  - "Add sliced chicken to the large salad bowl, toss all together with dressing."
legacyUrl: /dinner-1/chicken-shawarma-salad
---

One of my ALL TIME favorite dishes. So perfect in warm weather. Crunchy lettuce, flavorful, juicy chicken and a creamy lemon-tahini dressing to pull it all together. What could be better? Let’s jump in!
